matic dusk lighting, high contrast, and a desaturated warm color palette.\n[Shot 1] A wide shot establishes a ruined stone courtyard with broken columns and cracked marble floors at dusk, orange sunset light casting long shadows across the ground. <Subject 1>, the female warrior with short silver hair, a scar across her left cheek, dark leather armor, and a red cape, stands on the left facing <Subject 2>, the tall male villain with long black hair in a low ponytail, a gold eyepatch, and a long black coat with gold trim, who stands on the right resting his black cane with a silver skull handle on the ground. The camera holds a static shot as both figures remain motionless, staring each other down, wind stirring <Subject 1>'s red cape and the hem of <Subject 2>'s coat.\n[Shot 2] At 00:04.000, the shot cuts to a medium close-up of <Subject 1>, the silver-haired female warrior from Shot 1. Her right hand tightens on the longsword hilt at her waist and she draws the blade upward in a smooth controlled motion, the polished steel catching the orange dusk light with a bright gleam, her scarred face set in a determined expression, the red cape shifting behind her shoulders. The camera pushes in with small amplitude at slow speed as the blade reaches a ready position pointed toward <Subject 2>.\n[Shot 3] At 00:07.000, the shot cuts to a medium close-up of <Subject 2>, the tall male villain from Shot 1. He lifts his black cane with the silver skull handle and points it toward <Subject 1>, the skull's eye sockets beginning to glow with faint purple energy, his gold eyepatch catching the last of the sunset light, his long black coat swaying in the rising wind. The camera holds a static shot as the purple glow intensifies around the cane skull, ending on the tense standoff between the two figures.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nWind howls through the ruined stone courtyard while distant thunder rumbles on the horizon. The sharp metallic ring of a longsword being drawn cuts through the w